 ],
 "literal": "Like the speed of a released horse, / the lord of the land of hills with green bamboos touching the sky, / not knowing that we are pining for him, he too, / like a bull in the summer heat, / has grown thin, they say, desiring our excellent beauty.",
 "translation": "Like the speed of a horse released from its tether, is the lord of the hills where green bamboos touch the sky. Not knowing that we are pining for him, he too, like a bull suffering in the summer heat, has grown thin, they say, longing for our excellent beauty.",
 "modern": "அவிழ்த்து விடப்பட்ட குதிரையின் வேகத்தைப் போன்ற, வானத்தைத் தொடும் பசுமையான மூங்கில்களைக் கொண்ட மலைநாட்டின் தலைவன், நாம் அவனை நினைத்து வருந்துவதை அறியாதவனாய், தானும் கோடை காலத்து எருது இளைப்பது போல, நம்முடைய சிறந்த அழகை விரும்பி மெலிந்துவிட்டான் என்று கூறுகிறார்கள்.",
 "explanation": "The friend is speaking to the heroine to comfort her. She brings news that the hero is also suffering from love-sickness just like the heroine. She describes the hero as the lord of the hills where green bamboos rise high with the speed of a released horse. Unaware that the heroine is pining for him, the hero himself has grown thin like a bull suffering in the harsh summer heat, longing for her excellent beauty. This Kuriñci landscape imagery of the high hills and the suffering bull reflects the intensity of their mutual longing.",
